
## OpenAPI

```bash
ferrum-alloy openapi export --manifest ferrum-service.toml --output openapi.json
ferrum-alloy openapi export --manifest ferrum-service.toml --output openapi.json --check
```

The document is served on the management listener at `/openapi.json` (token-protected).

### AI agents

`get_item` is offered to AI agents as a read-only MCP tool. Its `#[utoipa::path]` declares `AgentTool::expose()`, and `[agents]` in `ferrum-service.toml` is enabled, so the exported document carries the `x-ferrum-mcp` extension that Ferrum Edge reads on `POST /api-specs`. Nothing else is exposed.

To try it through Edge, publish the exported document with `POST /api-specs` on Edge's admin API (see Ferrum Edge's `docs/api_specs.md`). Edge needs the proxy as `x-ferrum-proxy`, with the listen path from `ferrum-service.toml`, and the root `servers` reset to `/`, because Edge builds each tool's path from the listen path, then the server URL, then the path (keeping the exported `servers` would double the prefix):

```bash
jq '. + {"x-ferrum-proxy": {id: "{{name}}", listen_path: "/{{name}}", strip_listen_path: true,
      backend_scheme: "http", backend_host: "SERVICE_HOST", backend_port: 8080}}
    | .servers = [{url: "/"}]' openapi.json > edge-spec.json
curl -sS -X POST "$EDGE_ADMIN_URL/api-specs" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $EDGE_ADMIN_TOKEN" -H 'X-Ferrum-Namespace: ferrum' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' --data-binary @edge-spec.json
```

Replace `SERVICE_HOST` with the address Edge reaches this service at. Edge then serves MCP at `/{{name}}/mcp` on its proxy listener. Create an item first (the `POST /items` call under Run). After an MCP `initialize`, a `tools/call` of `{{name}}.get_item` with the arguments `{"id": 1}` runs `GET /items/1` against this service and returns that item. An id the service does not know, such as `{"id": 999}`, comes back as a tool error (`isError: true`, `HTTP 404 Not Found`) carrying the documented Problem Details body.
